<title>USA: Egypt order not affecting US grain exports so far.</title>
<headline>Egypt order not affecting US grain exports so far.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Existing Egyptian export business with the United States has not yet been affected by an Egyptian state decree barring imports of genetically altered grains and soybeans, several U.S. exporters said.</p>
<p>&quot;It's no big deal but it is a hassle,&quot; one major U.S. wheat exporter told Reuters. &quot;We are working on the language with them.&quot;</p>
<p>Egypt's Ministry of Health issued a decree dated July 1 that imported grains and soybeans meant for human consumption must be accompanied by a certificate which proves genetic engineering was not used in their production.</p>
</text>
